# Extra kernel configuration for the OnePlus 15 (infiniti) OSS kernel.
#
# Why CONFIG_TMPFS_XATTR=y
# -----------------------
# The GKI/ACK defconfig enables CONFIG_TMPFS=y but never mentions TMPFS_XATTR,
# and fs/Kconfig declares it as:
#
#     config TMPFS_XATTR
#         bool "Tmpfs extended attributes"
#         depends on TMPFS
#         default n
#
# so it ends up 'n' in the built kernel. PixelOS/LineageOS user space -- and
# modules that put an overlay or per-file metadata on tmpfs (Mountify, some
# KernelSU module layouts, Android's own selinux xattrs on /dev) -- need the
# tmpfs xattr handlers.
#
# Where these lines go (two places, on purpose)
# ---------------------------------------------
# .ci/20-config.sh applies this fragment to BOTH config surfaces, because in
# this workspace they control different things:
#
#   1. kernel/platform/kernel-6.12/common/arch/arm64/configs/gki_defconfig
#      The image that boots is //common:kernel_aarch64, built from here. The
#      device sets BOARD_USES_GENERIC_KERNEL_IMAGE := true and vendor/lineage's
#      kernel.mk hands the ROM out/dist/Image, which is that GKI image. So a
#      kernel option must be set here or it does not exist at runtime.
#      (.ci/patch-defconfig.py)
#
#   2. vendor/oneplus/sm8850/configs/canoe_perf.bzl
#      The Qualcomm kleaf defconfig dict. It drives the vendor DDK modules and
#      device trees (kleaf-scripts/modules_register.bzl -> canoe_perf_merged_defconfig
#      -> dtbs.bzl post_defconfig_fragments) and never reaches that kernel binary.
#      All vendor code on this device is built as loadable modules, which is why
#      "audio and display built from source" shows up as .ko in vendor_dlkm.
#      (.ci/apply-config.py)
#
# Run 38772010956 is the proof: patching only the dict left kleaf's dist/.config
# with CONFIG_TMPFS_XATTR=y and CONFIG_ARCH_CANOE=y, while the config embedded in
# out/dist/Image had no CLO symbol at all.
#
# Placement matters for the GKI defconfig
# ---------------------------------------
# kleaf runs `savedefconfig` on the built config and compares it line by line
# with gki_defconfig, failing with
#     ERROR: savedefconfig does not match common/arch/arm64/configs/gki_defconfig
# savedefconfig emits options in Kconfig traversal order, not alphabetically, so
# appending a line at the end of the file is rejected even though Kbuild would
# honour it (that is exactly how run 39028772560 failed). '# @after SYMBOL' tells
# .ci/patch-defconfig.py where a new line belongs; savedefconfig wants
# CONFIG_TMPFS_XATTR directly after CONFIG_TMPFS.
#
# Add further options with normal .config syntax; '=y', '=m', '="string"' and
# '# CONFIG_FOO is not set' are all understood. Use '# @after' whenever the
# option is new to gki_defconfig.
# @after CONFIG_TMPFS
CONFIG_TMPFS_XATTR=y
